/// Platform application configuration
/// Used by generate-k8s.rb to generate manifests from scala-play-app template
///
/// Load balancer managed via doctl:
///   Name: platform-lb
///   Certificate: idempotent-io-ssl-certificate (a8487391-c0d5-4a33-9ded-408fea25b075)
///   Hostname: idempotent.io
///   Targets: droplets tagged `web-lb-target` (auto-tracks pool replacement)

module platform

appName = "platform"
appPort = 9300
webMemory = "4400Mi"
javaAgent = "/opt/newrelic/newrelic.jar"

// Off for the same reason acumen is, and now MEASURED rather than argued
// (ISS-1112). Distributed tracing exists to correlate one request across
// services. Over the 24h to 2026-08-08, on account 7724695:
//
//   FROM Span SELECT count(*) FACET appName, parent.app SINCE 1 day ago
//     platform-web  parent.app = null  1,681,090
//     platform-job  parent.app = null    123,266
//
// `parent.app` is null on EVERY span in both tiers — not a majority, all of
// them. No trace in this account has ever crossed a service boundary, because
// platform-web and platform-job do not call each other over HTTP (work reaches
// the job tier through the tasks table) and nothing else instrumented exists to
// call. Faceting span category the same way says the same thing from the other
// side: 1,506,398 of 1,681,128 web spans are `generic`, i.e. in-process.
//
// What that bought: TracingBytes was 31.0 GB of the 77.0 GB the account ingested
// in the trailing 30 days — 40% of the bill — against a 100 GB/month free-tier
// ceiling August 2026 projected to reach 87% of.
//
// Removing it drops the run rate from 2.80 to ~1.77 GB/day, so a FULL month at
// that rate is ~55 GB and a trailing 30 days is ~46 GB. August itself lands
// around 63 GB rather than 87 — the 22.2 GB the month had already spent by the
// 8th is not refundable, which is why the check fires at 85% and not at the
// ceiling. That is headroom for acumen's newly-attached agent (ISS-1070) AND
// for the ~+5 GB/month trend that reaches 100 on its own by November.
//
// What it does NOT cost, checked rather than assumed:
//   - Errors. TransactionError carries class, message and stack trace and is
//     unaffected — 4,358 errors / 30 days across both tiers, 0.005 GB total.
//     `daily-error-triage` queries Transaction, Log and TransactionError and
//     never Span.
//   - Slow routes. `daily-perf-prs` runs on `dev slow-routes`, which is
//     platform's own data, not NewRelic.
//   - Heap/OOM. `platform-memory-improvement` queries Log.
//   - Transaction traces, which the agent still records; only span events stop.
// No playbook, rule or script in any repo queries `FROM Span`.
//
// Flip to true (one line, no other change) if platform ever grows a second
// instrumented service it actually calls, or a span-level investigation needs
// it for a window. Re-measure the bill any time with `dev newrelic ingest`.
distributedTracing = false
